{title: 340 - Jesus Saves}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #340 • JESUS SAVES • 15.15.16.15}
{lyricist: Priscilla J. Owens}
{composer: William J. Kirkpatrick}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 340}
{meta: tune JESUS SAVES}
{meta: meter 15.15.16.15}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]We have heard a joyful sound, Jesus [Am]saves, Jesus [F]saves;
[C/E]Spread the gladness [F]all around, Jesus [Am]saves, [C/G]Jesus [C7/Bb]saves;
[Bb]Bear the news to every land, [Dm/A]Climb the steeps [F/C]and cross [Am]the waves,
[C/G]Onward, 'tis [Am]our Lord's [Bb]command, Jesus [Am]saves, [C/G]Jesus [C7/Bb]saves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]ft it on the [Am]rolling [F]tide,
[F]Jesus saves, Jesus [Am]saves;
[C/E]Tell to [F]sinners, [Am]far [C/G]and [C7/Bb]wide,
[C/E]Jesus [F]saves, Jesus [C/G]saves;
[Bb]Sing, ye islands [Dm/A]of [F/C]the [Am]sea.
[Bb]Echo back, ye [Dm/A]ocean [F/C]caves,
[C/G]Earth shall [Am]keep [Bb]her [Am]jubilee,
[C/G]Jesus [Am]saves, [Bb]Jesus [C/G]saves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]ng above the [Am]battle's [F]strife,
[F]Jesus saves, Jesus [Am]saves;
[C/E]By His [F]death and [Am]endless [C7/Bb]life,
[C/E]Jesus [F]saves, Jesus [C/G]saves;
[Bb]Sing it softly [Dm/A]through [F/C]the [Am]gloom,
[Bb]When the heart for [Dm/A]mercy [F/C]craves,
[C/G]Sing [Am]in [Bb]triumph o'er [Am]the [C7/Bb]tomb,
[C/G]Jesus [Am]saves, [Bb]Jesus [C/G]saves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]ve the winds a [Am]mighty [F]voice,
[F]Jesus saves, Jesus [Am]saves;
[C/E]Let the [F]nations [Am]now [C/G]rejoice,
[C/E]Jesus [F]saves, Jesus [C/G]saves;
[Bb]Shout salvation [Dm/A]full [F/C]and [Am]free,
[Bb]Highest hills and [Dm/A]deepest [F/C]caves,
[C/G]This our [Am]song [Bb]of [Am]victory,
[C/G]Jesus [Am]saves, [Bb]Jesus [C/G]saves.
{end_of_verse}
